    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting explanations to individual levels, providing instant feedback, and making abstract concepts relatable through examples from hobbies or daily life. They could also bridge gaps for students like me, who lack formal education but crave deeper understanding. However, they shouldn’t replace human teachers—just complement them."
